  "blocks": {
    "\"Agent's rewriting whole files instead of patching. Output tokens cost roughly five times the input rate — get it emitting edits and the bill drops.\"": "“智能体在重写整个文件，而不是打补丁。输出 Token 的费率大约是输入的五倍——让它只输出编辑内容，账单就会下降。”",
    "\"The refactor session is burning through credit even though the inputs are small.\"": "“重构会话的输入明明很少，却在快速消耗额度。”",
    "Everything the model writes counts: the prose you read, the code it emits, tool calls, and any extended thinking the model does before answering. That last one surprises people — reasoning tokens are billed as output even when the harness often doesn't show them to you, and turning up effort spends more of them.": "模型写出的所有内容都会计入：你读到的文字、它生成的代码、<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool-call\">工具调用</a>，以及回答前进行的任何扩展思考。最后一项常让人意外——即使<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>通常不向你展示<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/reasoning-tokens\">推理 Token</a>，它们仍按输出计费；提高<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/effort\">推理投入</a>会消耗更多这类 Token。",
    "Output tokens also set the pace of a session. The model reads input quickly but generates output one token at a time, so when a turn feels slow, it's almost always the output being written, not the input being read. A long wait usually means a long answer is coming.": "输出 Token 也决定<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>的速度。模型读取输入很快，但输出必须逐个 Token 生成；因此，当一个<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/turn\">轮次</a>感觉很慢时，几乎总是因为模型正在写出输出，而不是正在读取输入。等待时间很长，通常意味着即将得到一个很长的回答。",
    "Tokens the model generates back. Billed at a higher rate than input tokens — commonly around five times the rate — since they cost more compute to produce.": "输出 Token 是<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/model\">模型</a>生成并返回的 Token。它们的费率高于<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/input-tokens\">输入 Token</a>——通常约为后者的五倍——因为生成输出需要更多计算。",
